# x + a with IEEE-like results: add_2_1, then the fix-up. a is guarded (rule R3)
# before the fix-up adds it; the core is called with a and guards it itself.
# The fix-up is that of milestone1.md, "IEEE-like results", with r0 = times_inf(t) (exact, so not
# a fused operation) for prod(t, const inf): |z0| is named az here, since a is the operand.
kernel:        add_2_1_full
input:         x = x0 x1
input:         a
output:        w = w0 w1
value:         x+a
requires:      canonical x
ensures:       extends w core=add_2_1 lead=add
min_precision: 3
source:        add_2_1, then the fix-up of IEEE-like results (Milestone 1 listing)
license:       core: as add_2_1; fix-up: MIT
status:        unverified
domain:        extended
ieee_status:   unverified
entry:         yes
cone_exempt:   the fix-up selects, after an explicit test that z0 is finite (f), between the core's result and the canonical form of t; F1 to F5 of milestone1.md, "IEEE-like results", state what comes out

g        = guard(a)
(z0, z1) = add_2_1(x0, x1, a)
t        = add(x0, g)
az       = abs(z0)
f        = lt(az, const inf)
r0       = times_inf(t)
n        = eq(r0, r0)
r1       = select(n, 0, r0)
w0       = select(f, z0, r0)
w1       = select(f, z1, r1)
